From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:19:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: keep L2F
 on

L2F (1.8 V) supplies the camera sensors' DOVDD and the lens actuator's
I/O, and it is also the pull-up supply of the camera I2C bus (i2c9,
SE at 0x884000). The cameras turn it on only while they are powered,
so the first transfer on the bus at boot runs with the pull-ups off:

  gpi 800000.dma-controller: Error in Transaction
  geni_i2c 884000.i2c: DMA txn failed:3
  geni_i2c 884000.i2c: GPI transfer failed: -5

Keep L2F always on, as stock does. SuperTurtleDev's iceland kernel
(patches/platform-sm8850-7.3/apply/0048, Yibo Wang) found the same and
notes that a transfer with the rail down can wedge the GENI / GPI
engine until a reboot.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index cf5758dcba37..7ac40870b192 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -902,6 +902,11 @@
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_AUTO>;
+			/*
+			 * Also the pull-up supply of the camera I2C bus (i2c9):
+			 * a transfer while it is off fails in the GENI / GPI engine
+			 */
+			regulator-always-on;
 			regulator-allow-set-load;
 			regulator-allowed-modes = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_LPM
 						   RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_AUTO>;
